  "rationale": "The representative prefix ends in an adjective, but the target is a noun; the same adjective-to-noun continuation recurs across the batch, including small pears/apples/needles, red apples/pears, sunny day, next time, and little village. Existing noun rules emphasize other contexts and leave these noun candidates weak. Add a bounded suffix rule to the observed noun roots, rather than conditioning on particular adjectives or copying whole prefixes. This generalizes to noun phrases with other adjectives. It may overpromote these nouns after predicative or sentence-final adjectives, and other noun continuations remain valid; replay and batch gates must assess the tradeoff.",
